            },
            "text": "Within it, the city of Bhubaneswar is found to be a confluence of Hindu, Buddhist and Jain heritage boasting of some of the finest Kalingan temples. With many 6th-13th century CE Hindu temples, which span the entire spectrum of Kalinga architecture, Bhubaneswar is often referred to as a \"Temple City of India\"."
